# pots v1.4 — a supine blood pressure reading, on its own.
#
# THE FHIR COMPONENT PATTERN. A blood pressure is one observation with two
# component values, not two observations: FHIR models it as an Observation whose
# fhir:component repeats, each component carrying its own code and quantity. That
# is what pots:BloodPressureMeasurementShape's single Violation constraint
# checks -- sh:path fhir:component, sh:minCount 1 -- and it is deliberately
# structural rather than numeric.
#
# WHAT IS NOT CHECKED HERE, AND WHY THAT MATTERS. Neither component's VALUE is
# validated by anything. pots.shapes.ttl defines pots:SystolicComponentShape
# (40-300 mmHg) and pots:DiastolicComponentShape (20-200 mmHg), and both are
# UNREACHABLE: neither carries sh:targetClass, and the file contains no sh:node
# site to reach them by. So a systolic of 900 mmHg validates exactly as cleanly
# as the 118 below, and this fixture cannot be written to prove otherwise. That
# is a spec defect, reported as jayostis/spec#40, and it is out of scope here --
# jayostis/conformance#10 is deliberately scoped to the five REACHABLE classes so
# that it does not wait on spec picking a route.
#
# It is stated here rather than left silent because the natural reading of a
# passing blood-pressure fixture is that the numbers were checked. They were not.
# When spec#40 lands, the negative fixtures for those ranges belong beside this
# one and this paragraph should be replaced by them.
#
# 118/76 supine: an unremarkable normotensive baseline. A POTS screening is about
# the heart rate response to standing, so a normal supine pressure is the
# expected accompaniment rather than an incidental choice.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix pots: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/pots/v1#> .
@prefix fhir: <http://hl7.org/fhir/> .
@prefix loinc: <http://loinc.org/rdf#> .
@prefix ucum: <http://unitsofmeasure.org/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:b0750004-0000-4a00-8000-000000002010> a pots:BloodPressureMeasurement ;
    fhir:component [
        fhir:code loinc:8480-6 ;
        fhir:valueQuantity [
            fhir:value "118.0"^^xsd:double ;
            fhir:unit "mmHg" ;
            fhir:code ucum:mm-Hg
        ]
    ] ;
    fhir:component [
        fhir:code loinc:8462-4 ;
        fhir:valueQuantity [
            fhir:value "76.0"^^xsd:double ;
            fhir:unit "mmHg" ;
            fhir:code ucum:mm-Hg
        ]
    ] ;
    pots:secondsSinceStand "0.0"^^xsd:double .
